<h1><span lang="EN-GB">Capture Static Points</span></h1>
<hr align="left" width="98.974%" size="6" class="whs3">
<p class="description"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> <span class="Command">Capture Static Points</span> <span lang="EN-GB">command captures a single point each time the switch '</span>B' <span lang="EN-GB">is depressed. Depressing switch '</span>A' <span lang="EN-GB">terminates single point capture.</span> This command is accessible from <span class="Path">System &gt; Performance Check Utilities &gt; Capture &gt; Static Points</span>. It is also accessible from <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>'Capture single points'</b></span> button on the toolbar.</p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">If</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold; font-style:italic;"><i><b>'</b></i></span><span><i style="font-weight:bold; font-style:italic;">Capture single points'</i></span> <span lang="EN-GB">is not selected, hold down the left mouse button on the current selection for a second to show up the drop-down toolbar. Select</span> <i style="font-style:normal;">Capture single points</i> <span lang="EN-GB">button from there.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="../images/capture_static_points.gif" width="766px" height="150px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This command is normally used to capture ball probe points on certain locations in order to establish local co-ordinate system  see Transformations</span><span lang="EN-GB">. The localiser should be still when the switch '</span>B' <span lang="EN-GB">is depressed. In this way the localiser can be used without the ModelMaker sensor to capture measurements.</span></p>
